---
import DirectoryLayout from "../layouts/DirectoryLayout.astro";
---

<DirectoryLayout
  heading="Editorial & Data Policy"
  subheading="Our standards for data accuracy, automated discovery, AI boundaries, and corrections."
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: "Home", item: "/" },
    { name: "Editorial Policy", item: "/editorial-policy" },
  ]}
  canonicalPath="/editorial-policy"
>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto space-y-8 text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">1. Data Sources & Discovery</h2>
      <p>
        Listings in this directory originate from three transparent sources:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-slate-600">
        <li><strong>Automated Public Web Discovery:</strong> Search indexing of publicly shared invite URLs across standard web platforms.</li>
        <li><strong>Direct Community Submissions:</strong> Submissions from community leaders and members via our submission form.</li>
        <li><strong>Curated Seed Indexes:</strong> Well-known open source and developer hubs manually added by editors.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">2. The Role of Artificial Intelligence</h2>
      <p>
        We utilize large language models (Google Gemini) exclusively for assisting with taxonomic categorization, extracting keyword tags, and formatting descriptions. 
      </p>
      <p class="font-semibold text-slate-900">
        Our strict AI rules prohibit:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1 text-slate-600">
        <li>Inventing community names, invite links, or founder names.</li>
        <li>Estimating or fabricating member counts or growth stats.</li>
        <li>Fabricating reviews or subjective ratings.</li>
        <li>Certifying financial safety or investment viability.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">3. Link Health & Dead Link Policy</h2>
      <p>
        We run automated link audits to check if invites remain active. If an invite fails or becomes unreachable, its status is cautiously transitioned to <code class="bg-slate-100 px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">unknown</code> and then <code class="bg-slate-100 px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">dead</code> upon persistent 404 responses. Dead listings are kept temporarily with clear warnings or removed to prevent broken user experiences.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">4. Corrections & Takedown Requests</h2>
      <p>
        If you are the owner of a community and wish to update listing information or request immediate removal from the directory, please use our <a href="/report" class="text-emerald-600 font-semibold hover:underline">Report / Request form</a> or email our team. Requests are processed promptly.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</DirectoryLayout>
